+| **Date format** | How every user-visible date is written: **DD/MM/YYYY** (the default — Israel's civil order), **MM/DD/YYYY** or **YYYY-MM-DD**. Applies everywhere a date shows — the NOTAM / SIGMET / AIRMET **Updated** lines, the flight-plan date — while the time stays Zulu. File names and the filed-plan fields keep the ISO form. Persists to `navaid.dateFormat`. |
 | **Default speed (kt)** | Seed speed for a leg with no earlier leg to copy from — set it once for your aircraft. Drives the `defaultLegSpeedKt` tuning key and outranks the remote config, so it survives a reload. Accepts 20–400; anything else snaps back to the value in force. Persists to `navaid.defaultSpeed`. **↻** beside it returns to the default — the gist's speed if it sets one, else the built-in — and moves the legs that follow it; dimmed when the default is already in force. |
